[{:db/id -1
  :adr/id "adr-2800010600-gftd-ai-deprecation-and-magatama-host-sdk"
  :adr/title "gftd.ai is deprecated; and what deleting magatama-host-sdk actually costs"
  :adr/status "accepted"
  :adr/date "2026-09-02"
  :adr/body "## Two owner instructions, 2026-09-02

1. `gftdcojp/magatama-host-sdk` may be deleted.
2. **gftd.ai is deprecated; refactor everything onto itonami.cloud.**

This ADR records what was measured before acting, including a correction to a
framing this session itself produced.

## Correction: \"six symbols\" was misleading

The four appviews that depend on the SDK import exactly six names, and this
session reported that as \"a six-symbol shell\". That is true of the IMPORT
SURFACE and false about the WORK:

| symbol | where | size |
|---|---|---|
| `asAgentTool` / `withCapabilityTags` / `withOCELEvent` | `app-options.ts` | 3 lines each, `CommandOption` setters, touch no database |
| `nsid` | already exists in `kotoba-lang/xrpc` (`@etzhayyim/xrpc`, `./nsid`) | nothing to move |
| **`createWorkerExport`** | `index.ts` | calls `createDefaultHostSDK` |
| **`HostSDK`** | `index.ts` | the interface over the whole host |

`createDefaultHostSDK` builds `app.ts` (993 lines), `host-imports.ts` (1,289),
the PDS `XrpcClient`, the Hono router and the WIT export surface
(`httpHandler` / `wHandler` / `serveHandler` / `shinkaHandler`).

**The SDK is 67 files, 68,345 lines.** Two of the six symbols ARE that. Moving
them is moving the host runtime, not extracting a shell. The option chosen on
2026-09-02 (\"move the six symbols first, then delete\") was chosen on the
misleading half of that description.

## Every dependent is dead

| appview | route | measured |
|---|---|---|
| `cloud-itonami/media` | media.itonami.cloud | **NXDOMAIN** |
| `cloud-itonami/news` | news.gftd.ai | timeout |
| `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media` | media.gftd.ai | timeout |
| `gftdcojp/mamori` | mamori.gftd.ai | timeout |

Control: `gftd.ai` itself answers 200 from the same client, so the timeouts are
the hosts and not the network.

**No itonami.cloud successor exists.** `itonami.cloud/media`, `/news` and
`/mamori` return 200, but so does `/definitely-not-a-page`, and all four
responses are the same SHA-256 as the home page — the SPA catch-all
(`/* /index.html 200`). The same trap this session hit at `/install.sh`, where
a catch-all 200 would have fed the home page into `sh`. **A 200 from this site
is not evidence a surface exists; compare the body hash to the home page.**

## What follows

Nothing is live, and the SDK exists only to serve those four. Porting 68,345
lines of host runtime into kotoba-lang so that four dead appviews keep
building is work with no consumer. If media / news / mamori are wanted on
itonami.cloud, that is a build on the itonami stack — which is live and
already serving — not a port of the gftd-era host SDK.

So the recommendation is **retire rather than migrate**, and the sequencing
question for the owner is whether the four appviews are retired with it.

## Blocked on the owner either way

The workspace token carries `gist, read:org, repo`. GitHub requires
**`delete_repo`** for `DELETE /repos/{owner}/{repo}`, so this agent cannot
delete the repository regardless of the decision. Repository deletion is also
outside the standing authorization in CLAUDE.md.

## The gftd.ai deprecation surface

**21 wrangler configs across 20 repositories** route to gftd.ai:

    cloud-itonami/media  cloud-itonami/news  gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media
    gftdcojp/apex  gftdcojp/engi  gftdcojp/fashion  gftdcojp/itad
    gftdcojp/mamori  gftdcojp/shirabe  net-kotobase/engine
    net-kotobase/ipfs  network-awai/cloud-murakumo
    network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api
    network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api-categories-deploy
    network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api-codex-categories
    network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api-codex-categories-final
    network-awai/cloud-murakumo-llms-codex  network-awai/local-murakumo
    network-awai/local-murakumo-fastmtp  network-awai/local-murakumo-runpod5090

Four of them are the magatama dependents above. **Liveness was measured only
for those four** — the other sixteen are unmeasured, and the same catch-all
trap applies to any of them fronted by a SPA, so check body hashes rather than
status codes. Do not read this list as sixteen live services needing a port.

The surface index (`90-docs/surface/surface.datoms.edn`) also still carries
`news.gftd.ai -> orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-news`, a fifth gftd-era repo not in the
wrangler list.\n\n## 2026-09-02 実施分と、この ADR 自身の訂正\n\n### 訂正 1: `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media` は別 repo ではない\n\nThis ADR listed it as a fourth dependent with its own dead route\n`media.gftd.ai`. It is **the same repository as `cloud-itonami/media`** —\n`GET /repos/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media` answers `full_name: cloud-itonami/media`.\nThe transfer already happened and GitHub redirects the old name.\n\nWhat produced the wrong reading is a **stale duplicate checkout**:\n`orgs/gftdcojp/ai-gftd-media` sits at 2026-07-19 content, is registered in\n`manifest/west.yml` under NO name, and is clean with no unique commits. Two\ncheckouts of one repo at different pins look exactly like two near-identical\nrepos — the 9-line diff that made it read as a duplicate was six weeks of\ndrift, not a fork. So the dependent count is **three distinct repos**, not\nfour, and there is nothing to migrate here: the move is done.\n\n### 訂正 2: `generation.murakumo.cloud` is not a successor\n\n`murakumo-generation.gftd.ai` is live (403, auth-gated) and\n`generation.murakumo.cloud` answers 200, which reads like the obvious\ndestination. It is not: its body is **byte-identical to `murakumo.cloud/`**\n— the marketing page, not a generation API. Pointing a production generation\nupstream there would have failed silently.\n\nThat is the third time in this session the same trap produced a confident\nwrong answer (`/install.sh`, `itonami.cloud/media|news|mamori`, and here).\n**On these zones a 200 is not evidence a surface exists. Compare the body\nhash against the zone root and against a path known not to exist.**\n\n### Landed\n\n- `cloud-itonami/news` → `news.itonami.cloud` (ef299ba2). Not just the route:\n  `news.core/writer-did-for-source` minted `did:web:news.gftd.ai:writer:{slug}`\n  for every attributed source, and a did:web resolves from the host inside it,\n  so the constant had to move or mint unresolvable DIDs. 20 occurrences across\n  core/schema/taxonomy/tests/fixtures. `src/app.ts` was also returning\n  `movedTo: \"media.gftd.ai\"` to callers while media had been at\n  media.itonami.cloud for three weeks. Config only — not deployed.\n- `gftdcojp/shirabe` (dbcd917c): worker `ai-gftd-project-shirabe` → `shirabe`;\n  dropped `SHIRABE_DAEMON_URL`, which pointed at a dead host AND overrode the\n  code's own `?? \"http://127.0.0.1:8765\"` localhost default.\n\n### Already clean\n\n`gftdcojp/mamori` and `gftdcojp/engi` — other sessions had already dropped\ntheir routes and DIDs. Their remaining `gftd` strings are the\n`@gftd/magatama-host-sdk` dependency, provenance in MIGRATION.edn, and NSIDs.\n\n### Not touched, deliberately: `ai.gftd.apps.*`\n\nThese are **AT Protocol XRPC method identifiers** — wire contract with\ncallers, not decoration. `mamori`'s own README states the rule: \"The\n`ai.gftd.apps.mamori.*` NS is a leftover protocol identifier; do not rename\nit.\" `ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.datomic` is additionally translated server-side by\nkotobase.net, and this session established that kotobase.net cannot be probed\nfor method routing — it returns 401 for a method that does not exist as\nreadily as for one that does. Renaming a namespace that a live server\ntranslates, without being able to test it, is a data-plane break dressed as a\nstring cleanup.\n\n### Still open\n\n- `itad.gftd.ai` (200, genuinely live) and `murakumo-generation.gftd.ai` (403,\n  live, no verified successor) — both need a destination decision and a deploy\n  window, not a config sweep.\n- `fashion.gftd.ai` (dead) — same treatment as shirabe, not yet done.\n- `auth.gftd.ai` — a 19th host, found only because `authn.gftd.ai` 301s to it."}]
